WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.026
Thousands of kilometres away,

2
00:00:02.026 --> 00:00:03.106
in the Pacific Ocean,

3
00:00:03.106 --> 00:00:04.650
a patch of sea warms up by

4
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.125
a degree or two.

5
00:00:06.125 --> 00:00:08.491
And farmers in India start to worry.

6
00:00:08.891 --> 00:00:10.331
In a normal year,

7
00:00:10.331 --> 00:00:12.746
trade winds push warm surface water west

8
00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.452
across the Pacific.

9
00:00:14.452 --> 00:00:17.192
Warm, moist air rises over that water

10
00:00:17.192 --> 00:00:18.618
and brings rain.

11
00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.517
In an El Niño year,

12
00:00:20.517 --> 00:00:22.363
the trade winds weaken.

13
00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:23.965
The warm water spreads east,

14
00:00:23.965 --> 00:00:25.428
towards South America,

15
00:00:25.428 --> 00:00:27.492
and the rising air moves with it.

16
00:00:27.892 --> 00:00:29.935
Over India, more air sinks instead of

17
00:00:29.935 --> 00:00:31.143
rising.

18
00:00:31.143 --> 00:00:33.093
So the monsoon is often weaker,

19
00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:35.019
and droughts become more likely.

20
00:00:35.419 --> 00:00:37.044
But not always.

21
00:00:37.044 --> 00:00:38.287
In nineteen ninety-seven,

22
00:00:38.287 --> 00:00:40.214
a very strong El Niño came,

23
00:00:40.214 --> 00:00:43.070
and India's monsoon was still normal.

24
00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:45.379
The Indian Ocean had its own say.

25
00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:47.252
Its opposite is La Niña,

26
00:00:47.252 --> 00:00:49.040
when the eastern Pacific turns cooler than

27
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.271
usual.

28
00:00:50.271 --> 00:00:52.163
La Niña years often bring India a

29
00:00:52.163 --> 00:00:53.429
good monsoon.

30
00:00:53.429 --> 00:00:55.089
The swing comes every two to seven

31
00:00:55.089 --> 00:00:56.063
years.

32
00:00:56.463 --> 00:00:57.543
For GS One:

33
00:00:57.543 --> 00:00:59.424
El Niño warms the eastern Pacific,

34
00:00:59.424 --> 00:01:00.457
weakens the trade winds,

35
00:01:00.457 --> 00:01:02.024
and often, but not always,

36
00:01:02.024 --> 00:01:03.683
weakens India's monsoon.

